---

This project is a derivative work that incorporates code and methodology from
the following MIT-licensed open source projects. Their copyright notices are
retained below.

1. ai-check  --  https://github.com/HoneyMeta/ai-check-skills
   The detection engine (scripts/aigc_detox_lcw_scan.py), the rewrite guard
   (scripts/aigc_detox_lcw_rewrite.py), and the HTML/PDF report skeleton
   originate from this project.

2. humanizer-zh-academic  --  https://github.com/redbaronyyyyy-eng/humanizer-zh-academic
   The 16 AI-writing-pattern taxonomy, before/after rewrite examples, register
   calibration table, and noise-retention principle in references/patterns.md
   originate from this project.

3. aigc-detector  --  https://github.com/free-revalution/AIGC-Detector-Pro
   The five-dimension semantic diagnostic vocabulary originates from this
   project. Its numeric scoring scheme was deliberately not adopted; see
   references/benchmark.md section 4 for the measured reason.

4. chinese-thesis-workbench  --  https://github.com/ZyhSechub/chinese-thesis-workbench-skill
   Used as a workflow reference only. Its AIGC style analyzer was evaluated and
   rejected (7/6 error on the benchmark set); no code from it is included.

5. aigc-down-skill  --  https://github.com/Yezery/aigc-down-skill
   Archived as a sibling variant for reference only; no code from it is
   included.

Additions original to this project: the post-rewrite verification loop
(scripts/aigc_detox_lcw_compare.py) and the clause-level rhythm fallback
(clause_rhythm_features in scripts/aigc_detox_lcw_scan.py).
